Does the review sheet tell the truth about polarity? Work it out yourself from
the evidence below before reading the review's verdicts.

For each polarised part, the datasheet research says which footprint pad is
the cathode or pin 1. The built board says which net each physical pad is on.
The intended circuit says which net the cathode or pin 1 must be on. A part is
reversed when the pad the datasheet marks sits on a net the circuit does not
intend for it, even if the part's pin names look right.

